    "core:description": "hackriff fixture capture-2026-09-15-fm-band: 45.0 s of the FM broadcast band as sampled at this site (HackRF One, 100.800 MHz centre, 2.4 Msps, LNA 32 / VGA 30 / amp on, antenna unknown (as attached by user; not changed)). Requested span 99.600-102.000 MHz, single tune, no retune. Receive-only; truth is PHY metadata only. THE TRUTH ANNOTATIONS ARE MEASURED (T-289, 2026-09-16): an analysis pass over the samples annotated three emissions (WFM broadcast at 101.298663 MHz and 99.699944 MHz, both carrying a 19 kHz stereo pilot, and an unidentified 28 kHz narrowband emission at 100.465339 MHz) and two receiver artefacts (the 10 MHz reference harmonic at 99.999572 MHz and the DC offset at the tuner centre). Each annotation records the measurement that justifies it. The frequencies this capture README anticipated were each measured and are not what it expected: the stations are elsewhere, the ''steady carrier'' at 99.99 MHz is a receiver spur, and 100.3 MHz was silent for all 45 s. Windows measured to be silent are recorded in the scenario annotation as measured_absent and carry no annotation of their own.",
